# eve-chat-template reference mirror

Brain’s chat UI is adapted from [vercel-labs/eve-chat-template](https://github.com/vercel-labs/eve-chat-template), **without** Vercel Connect, Neon, Upstash, AI Gateway, or the template’s Vercel-tied auth stack. Brain uses self-hosted Better Auth for login (see `lib/auth/`).

## Local clone (required reference)

| Item | Value |
| --- | --- |
| Path | `/Users/dev/github/tmp/eve-chat-template` |
| Upstream | `https://github.com/vercel-labs/eve-chat-template` |
| Design | `docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-29-brain-chat-ui-design.md` |
| Plans | `docs/superpowers/plans/README.md` |
| OpenSpec change | `openspec/changes/add-brain-chat-ui/` |
| OpenSpec specs | `openspec/specs/` |

Before implementing or porting chat UI, connections menus, message/tool rendering, HITL, or shell chrome:

1. Prefer reading files from `/Users/dev/github/tmp/eve-chat-template/...` over guessing.
2. If the clone is missing or stale, refresh it:

```bash
mkdir -p /Users/dev/github/tmp
if [ -d /Users/dev/github/tmp/eve-chat-template/.git ]; then
  git -C /Users/dev/github/tmp/eve-chat-template fetch origin
  git -C /Users/dev/github/tmp/eve-chat-template checkout main
  git -C /Users/dev/github/tmp/eve-chat-template pull --ff-only origin main
else
  git clone https://github.com/vercel-labs/eve-chat-template.git /Users/dev/github/tmp/eve-chat-template
fi
git -C /Users/dev/github/tmp/eve-chat-template rev-parse --short HEAD
```

3. When pulling new upstream ideas into Brain, **copy patterns then strip** auth/DB/Connect — never reintroduce forbidden Vercel infra (see `.cursor/rules/no-vercel-infra.mdc`).

## High-value template paths

- `app/_components/agent-chat.tsx` — eve client bridge (Brain: ephemeral only; no persist actions)
- `components/chat/{composer,conversation,message,markdown,sidebar,integrations-menu}.tsx`
- `next.config.ts` — `withEve()`
- `docs/how-the-chatbot-works.md` — architecture explanation (ignore Neon/auth sections for Brain v1)
